(6633059, 990241, 141319, '<td valign="top">Such a tranquil picture! But for me the straight horizon is distracting. I would have prefered no horizon line, i.e the "fog" moving into the black and the black extending to the edge of the picture. I would like to know if this is a "real" landscape somewhere and you played with exposure, or if you set this up and/or photoshopped it?</td>', 'Such a tranquil picture! But for me the straight horizon is distracting. I would have prefered no horizon line, i.e the "fog" moving into the black and the black extending to the edge of the picture. I would like to know if this is a "real" landscape somewhere and you played with exposure, or if you set this up and/or photoshopped it?', '2012-01-03 14:44:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6633060, 990364, 141319, '<td valign="top">Very powerful message in this picture. Good composition, great light. The eye is really drawn to the horrible smoke cloud.</td>', 'Very powerful message in this picture. Good composition, great light. The eye is really drawn to the horrible smoke cloud.', '2012-01-03 14:47:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6633065, 990221, 141319, '<td valign="top">How did you manage to get that shot? The red is amazing and sets off the lizard beautifully against the green leave(s) in the background. Beautiful photograph.</td>', 'How did you manage to get that shot? The red is amazing and sets off the lizard beautifully against the green leave(s) in the background. Beautiful photograph.', '2012-01-03 14:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6633071, 990477, 141319, '<td valign="top">It took me a while to see why you called this "Winter *rider*...". The person should have really been in the lighter part of the pciture, you can hardly make him out. IMO this would have been a nice enough shot just as a seascape :-). The image seems a bit "grainy"? Did you have to use a very high ISO?</td>', 'It took me a while to see why you called this "Winter *rider*...". The person should have really been in the lighter part of the pciture, you can hardly make him out. IMO this would have been a nice enough shot just as a seascape :-). The image seems a bit "grainy"? Did you have to use a very high ISO?', '2012-01-03 14:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6633076, 990460, 104230, '<td valign="top">Fascinating, and a lovely tone.  I especially like that the undergrowth overlapping the edges of the steps creates a feel of the lower steps meandering slightly to right and left rather than just going straight up.  Well seen.</td>', 'Fascinating, and a lovely tone.  I especially like that the undergrowth overlapping the edges of the steps creates a feel of the lower steps meandering slightly to right and left rather than just going straight up.  Well seen.', '2012-01-03 14:58:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6633078, 988839, 141319, '<td valign="top">.. and so is this picture :-). Beautiful light and colours in sky and water. Great Silhouettes. I am not sold on the black beach in front though. Without it the people jumping "above water" would have bprobably also been a problem, but for me perhaps the lesser of the 2 evils :-). The horizon line should perhaps also be level.</td>', '.. and so is this picture :-). Beautiful light and colours in sky and water. Great Silhouettes. I am not sold on the black beach in front though. Without it the people jumping "above water" would have bprobably also been a problem, but for me perhaps the lesser of the 2 evils :-). The horizon line should perhaps also be level.', '2012-01-03 14:59:04.000000', NULL, 1),
