(6637812, 990649, 30364, '<td valign="top">Well, yes he is.  I like this for it''s strangeness in both idea and execution.  I especially like the fact that the TV is clearer and more assured of its relevance than is the protagonist, Jedermann.  The TV seems to be sitting in judgement of him, which is probably as you intended.  Apt.  Thank you, and bravo for attempting something as ambitious as this.  Your exciting prize is an Order of the Thumb. Lucky you!<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Well, yes he is.  I like this for it''s strangeness in both idea and execution.  I especially like the fact that the TV is clearer and more assured of its relevance than is the protagonist, Jedermann.  The TV seems to be sitting in judgement of him, which is probably as you intended.  Apt.  Thank you, and bravo for attempting something as ambitious as this.  Your exciting prize is an Order of the Thumb. Lucky you!', '2012-01-07 16:16:54.000000', NULL, 1),
