(6639024, 990624, 104230, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> the shrouds are particularly fetching against everything else shrouded. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks. I like that slightly lighter area behind the shrouds and made sure to keep that feature during the processing.  The sun was starting to break through.  We, that''s <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30861" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bear_music</a> and me, were right to go to the nearest place when the fog came because unlike early morning fog which you can kind of predict how long it will last based on the angle and intensity of the sun, this mid-day fog only lasted a very short time.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-25 08:37:03.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: the shrouds are particularly fetching against everything else shrouded.   Thanks. I like that slightly lighter area behind the shrouds and made sure to keep that feature during the processing.  The sun was starting to break through.  We, that''s  bear_music and me, were right to go to the nearest place when the fog came because unlike early morning fog which you can kind of predict how long it will last based on the angle and intensity of the sun, this mid-day fog only lasted a very short time.', '2012-01-08 16:01:08.000000', '2012-02-25 08:37:03.000000', 0),
